IMPORT prelude

-- Income Tax Act (R.S.C., 1985, c. 1 (5th Supp.)) -- the indexed amounts, as a dated table.
--
-- The Act states its dollar amounts in base-year figures and adjusts them every year: s 117.1(1) to (4) for the brackets
-- of s 117(2), the credit amounts of ss 118 and 118.3, the Canada workers benefit (s 122.7) and Part I.2; s 122.61(5)
-- and (7) for the Canada child benefit. The Act does not print the adjusted figures, and the base year of each amount
-- is set by amending Acts that are not deposited. So the adjusted figures are taken from the Canada Revenue Agency's
-- table "Indexation adjustment for personal income tax and benefit amounts" (page dated 2026-03-12), deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/cra-indexation-adjustment-2026.txt. It is not law: it is the CRA's statement of the
-- adjustment. Only the 2026 column is used.
--
-- The amounts the Act states without indexation are used as the Act states them, in ita-individual.l4: the pension
-- credit's $2,000 (s 118(3)), the CWB's $3,000 and $1,150 thresholds and its 27% and 15% rates, and the GST/HST credit
-- amounts of s 122.5(3.005), which s 117.1(2)(m.1) indexes only "for a taxation year that begins after 2026".
--
-- Read with the Unofficial-version notice in SOURCE-LICENSE.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Indexed amounts (s 117.1, s 122.61(5)), from the CRA's table`

-- The tax side, for a taxation year (amounts take effect on 1 January, per the table's preamble).
DECLARE `Indexed amounts for a taxation year` HAS
    -- s 117(2): "the amount determined for the taxation year in respect of" $57,375, $114,750, $177,882 and $253,414
    `the first bracket threshold`                     IS A NUMBER
    `the second bracket threshold`                    IS A NUMBER
    `the third bracket threshold`                     IS A NUMBER
    `the fourth bracket threshold`                    IS A NUMBER
    -- s 118(1.1): A ($12,298 as adjusted) and F(d) ($15,000 as adjusted)
    `the basic personal amount's A`                   IS A NUMBER
    `the basic personal amount's F`                   IS A NUMBER
    -- s 118(1), descriptions of C and D: $2,150 as adjusted (the CRA calls it the Canada caregiver amount for children
    -- under 18, a dependant spouse or common-law partner, an eligible dependant)
    `the infirmity addition`                          IS A NUMBER
    -- s 118(2): $6,408 and $25,921 as adjusted
    `the age amount`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `the age amount's income threshold`               IS A NUMBER
    -- s 118(10): $1,000 as adjusted
    `the Canada employment amount`                    IS A NUMBER
    -- s 118.3(1): B ($6,000), C(a)(i) ($3,500) and C(a)(ii)(B) ($2,050), each as adjusted
    `the disability amount`                           IS A NUMBER
    `the child disability supplement`                 IS A NUMBER
    `the child care expenses threshold`               IS A NUMBER
    -- s 180.2(2), B(b): $50,000 as adjusted (s 117.1(2)(t))
    `the OAS recovery threshold`                      IS A NUMBER
    -- s 122.7(2): $1,395 and $2,403 in A; $22,944 and $26,177 in B; s 122.7(1.3): $14,000
    `the CWB maximum for a single individual`         IS A NUMBER
    `the CWB maximum for a family`                    IS A NUMBER
    `the CWB threshold for a single individual`       IS A NUMBER
    `the CWB threshold for a family`                  IS A NUMBER
    `the CWB secondary earner exemption`              IS A NUMBER
    -- s 122.7(3): $720 in C; $32,244 and $42,197 in D
    `the CWB disability supplement maximum`           IS A NUMBER
    `the CWB disability supplement threshold for a single individual` IS A NUMBER
    `the CWB disability supplement threshold for a family` IS A NUMBER

-- The 2026 column of the CRA's table.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Indexed amounts for a taxation year`
`the indexed amounts for the taxation year` year MEANS
    IF year EQUALS 2026
    THEN JUST (`Indexed amounts for a taxation year` WITH
        `the first bracket threshold`                     IS 58523
        `the second bracket threshold`                    IS 117045
        `the third bracket threshold`                     IS 181440
        `the fourth bracket threshold`                    IS 258482
        -- "Basic personal amount for individuals whose net income ... is greater than or equal to the amount at which the
        -- 33% tax bracket begins"
        `the basic personal amount's A`                   IS 14829
        -- "Basic personal amount (maximum) ... less than or equal to the amount at which the 29% tax bracket begins"
        `the basic personal amount's F`                   IS 16452
        `the infirmity addition`                          IS 2740
        `the age amount`                                  IS 9208
        `the age amount's income threshold`               IS 46432
        `the Canada employment amount`                    IS 1501
        `the disability amount`                           IS 10341
        `the child disability supplement`                 IS 6032
        `the child care expenses threshold`               IS 3533
        `the OAS recovery threshold`                      IS 95323
        `the CWB maximum for a single individual`         IS 1665
        `the CWB maximum for a family`                    IS 2869
        `the CWB threshold for a single individual`       IS 27392
        `the CWB threshold for a family`                  IS 31251
        `the CWB secondary earner exemption`              IS 16714
        `the CWB disability supplement maximum`           IS 860
        `the CWB disability supplement threshold for a single individual` IS 38495
        `the CWB disability supplement threshold for a family` IS 50377)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The Canada child benefit side, for the months of a benefit year. The table's preamble: increases for the CCB and
-- the child disability benefit "take effect on July 1"; its 2026 column is used for the months July 2026 to June 2027,
-- whose base taxation year (s 122.6) is 2025.
DECLARE `Indexed CCB amounts` HAS
    -- s 122.61(1), E(a) and E(b): $6,400 and $5,400 as adjusted
    `the amount for a child under six`                IS A NUMBER
    `the amount for a child aged six to seventeen`    IS A NUMBER
    -- s 122.61(1), Q: $30,000 and $65,000 as adjusted
    `the first income threshold`                      IS A NUMBER
    `the second income threshold`                     IS A NUMBER
    -- s 122.61(1), Q(c): $2,450, $4,725, $6,650 and $8,050 as adjusted
    `the base phase-out for one child`                IS A NUMBER
    `the base phase-out for two children`             IS A NUMBER
    `the base phase-out for three children`           IS A NUMBER
    `the base phase-out for four or more children`    IS A NUMBER
    -- s 122.61(1), N: $2,730 as adjusted (the CRA's "child disability benefit")
    `the child disability benefit amount`             IS A NUMBER

-- The month is given as a year and a month number (1 to 12).
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER, month IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Indexed CCB amounts`
`the indexed CCB amounts for the month` year month MEANS
    IF (year EQUALS 2026 AND month AT LEAST 7 AND month AT MOST 12) OR (year EQUALS 2027 AND month AT LEAST 1 AND month AT MOST 6)
    THEN JUST (`Indexed CCB amounts` WITH
        `the amount for a child under six`                IS 8157
        `the amount for a child aged six to seventeen`    IS 6883
        `the first income threshold`                      IS 38237
        `the second income threshold`                     IS 82847
        `the base phase-out for one child`                IS 3123
        `the base phase-out for two children`             IS 6022
        `the base phase-out for three children`           IS 8476
        `the base phase-out for four or more children`    IS 10260
        `the child disability benefit amount`             IS 3480)
    ELSE NOTHING
